{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBPiJDxyBXBQrjAWuoZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QKCPSqqB2p9XKHdMs28LK5","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Read source game reference pages","subagent_type":"web-fetch","prompt":"Read these public pages about the Wii game \"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\" and report what they actually say (say \"not stated\" for anything a page doesn't cover; don't fill in from memory):\n\n- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Second_Opinion\n- https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trauma_Center:_Under_the_Knife\n- https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Trauma_Center_Second_Opinion\n- https://gamesradar.com/trauma-center-second-opinion-review\n\nI need, as a compact factual digest (bullet points, under 500 words):\n1. Control scheme: how the Wii Remote pointer and Nunchuk stick are used, and how tools are selected.\n2. The complete list of surgical tools and what each does.\n3. The special ability (Healing Touch): what it does, how it is triggered, and how it differs between the two doctors.\n4. The operation structure: vitals, time limit, failure conditions, per-action ratings, and final rank letters.\n5. Story: setting, main characters, the disease and how its strains work, the antagonist group, how chapters are structured, and what Second Opinion added compared with the DS game.\n6. What reviewers say about tone and writing, and about difficulty.","run_in_background":false},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4948,"cache_read_input_tokens":234559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4948},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-