{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD3R4oWysoT3Z5uF1XZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PN9VY23yELR9C4wtu83X7X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b, count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) >= 1, 'MISSING: ' + a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b) if count == 0 else s.replace(a, b, count)\n\nsub(\"your brief names the dev folder, the final HTML file and the exit-interview file.\", \"your brief names the dev folder, the final HTML file and the exit interview file.\")\nsub(\"- **Timer:** per operation. Zero fails the operation. Bar stays visible and pulses under 30 s.\", \"- **Timer:** per operation. Zero fails the operation. It stays visible, and pulses under 30 s.\")\n\n# difficulty, retry\nsub(\"\"\"**Checkpoints:** every phase is a checkpoint. Failing offers *Retry phase*, *Restart operation*, *Quit*. Retrying a phase restores vitals to at least 60 and gives the phase a fresh time allowance. Phases must be self-contained: a phase's `spawn` lists everything it needs, so `skipTo(phase)` works for retry, dev mode and attract mode alike.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"New Game asks once, in Bea's voice (\"How much do you hate yourself, child?\"), and every chart can change it.\n\n**Checkpoints:** every phase is a checkpoint. Failing offers *Retry phase*, *Restart operation*, *Quit*. Retrying a phase restores vitals to at least 60, the timer to at least 90 s, and the score to the checkpoint's. Phases must be self-contained: a phase's `spawn` lists everything it needs, so `skipTo(phase)` works for retry, dev mode and attract mode alike. Use `ifMissing: true` for what an earlier phase normally leaves behind, such as clamps.\"\"\")\n\n# pads\nsub(\"\"\"**Rumble:** `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` if present, with a Settings toggle. Heartbeat double-pulse at low vitals, a tick per stitch, a click for clamps, a slam for Defib. Guard against a missing actuator; it can't be tested here beyond the guard.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Pads:** accept any pad the browser reports with `mapping === 'standard'`. Read `axes` and `buttons[i].value` directly. If the active pad disconnects mid-operation, pause.\n\n**Rumble:** `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` if present, with a Settings toggle. Heartbeat double-pulse at low vitals, a tick per stitch, a click for clamps, a slam for Defib. Guard against a missing actuator; it can't be tested here beyond the guard.\"\"\")\n\n# mouse\nsub(\"\"\"Mouse: hover moves the focus (there's always exactly one focused item), click confirms, wheel scrolls, RMB backs out.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Mouse: hover moves the focus (there's always exactly one focused item), click confirms, wheel scrolls, RMB backs out. In story scenes a click advances the line. In an operation, the wheel's slots and the site tabs are clickable, and the parallax follows the pointer.\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu |\", \"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu. Opens by itself when the tab is hidden (outside sessions) |\")\n\nsub(\"Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement,\", \"Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement,\")\n\nsub(\"| Face (code-driven from clips' events) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression changes |\", \"| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\")\n\n# on its own\nsub(\"\"\"\"On its own,\" a hub phrase, means outside a session: the page runs as a normal game, with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Your brief also says to follow the protocol \"for the game on its own\". In the hub's own check, \"on its own\" means the page opened outside a session, so that's what we mean too: a normal game with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\"\"\")\n\n# session snippet\nsub(\"\"\"  AIHub.on('time-up', finish);                             // within graceMs, host only\n  AIHub.on('end', stopEverything);                         // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n  (function pump() {\n    if (ended) return;\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\n  let ended = false;\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n  (function pump() {\n    if (ended) return;\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"\"\")\n\n# save\nsub(\"\"\"- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\n- Saves (`src/app/save.js`): progress, best ranks and settings in `localStorage`, wrapped in try/catch. In a session the game saves nothing.\"\"\")\n\n# accuracy of the claim\nsub(\"\"\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A prototype with this stack and these recipes passed the hub's harness at 2 and 4 players (bad network, a player leaving), host-leave and server scenarios, on WebGPU and without it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, the §14.3 message rates) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\"\"\")\n\n# install notes\nsub(\"\"\"Fonts: **Barlow Condensed** (500/600/700) for UI and dialogue, **Bangers** for comic lettering (both OFL; credit them on the About screen; about 22 KB each).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"npm warns about install scripts; esbuild works anyway. Don't run `playwright install`: the browsers are already here. Fonts: **Barlow Condensed** (500/600/700) for UI and dialogue, **Bangers** for comic lettering (both OFL; credit them on the About screen; about 22 KB each).\"\"\")\n\n# tests\nsub(\"\"\"Wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` (allow 300 s), and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and **no console line starting `[AIHub]`**. Use a 1280×860 viewport. Run with §16.3 flags and once without them. Then **on its own:**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` (allow 300 s), and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and **no console line starting `[AIHub]`**. Use a 1280×860 viewport. Run all five with the §16.3 flags, and the 4-player run once more without them (WebGL2). Then **on its own:**\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"\"\"- Dev mode: reachable from Pause; each tool runs once without error; a slider changes sim behavior live; Reset restores defaults exactly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Dev mode: reachable from Pause; each tool runs once without error; a slider changes sim behavior live; Reset restores defaults exactly. Every tuning ID is read somewhere in `src/` (no dead sliders).\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"\"\"One command: **`node tests/run-all.mjs [sim|browser|hub]`**. It prints only failures and a one-line count, and exits non-zero on failure. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Run one browser at a time; \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out, so run fewer. No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. All files stay inside the dev folder.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"One command: **`node tests/run-all.mjs [sim|browser|hub]`**. It prints only failures and a one-line count, and exits non-zero on failure. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Run one browser at a time; \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out, so run fewer. No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. All files stay inside the dev folder. Keep a running tally of the bugs your tests catch and which were critical: your brief's Testing Feedback asks for those counts.\"\"\")\n\n# about\nsub(\"\"\"Give each its own pages at ten-foot size: one short answer per page position, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: authored-by model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Give each block its own pages at ten-foot size, a few short answers per page, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: the model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('ok', s.count('\\n'), 'lines')\nEOF\ngrep -n -E \"Target closed|hub:webgpu|any-pointer|Dies Irae|§12|§13\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-90 | head -20","description":"Apply review fixes to the plan text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11196,"cache_read_input_tokens":362625,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11196},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"91bf54de-0163-45e8-912e-1cfbeb3375cb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:39.460Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD3QcXVGBtxX75JddgE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PN9VY23yELR9C4wtu83X7X":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b, count=1):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) >= 1, 'MISSING: ' + a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b) if count == 0 else s.replace(a, b, count)\n\nsub(\"your brief names the dev folder, the final HTML file and the exit-interview file.\", \"your brief names the dev folder, the final HTML file and the exit interview file.\")\nsub(\"- **Timer:** per operation. Zero fails the operation. Bar stays visible and pulses under 30 s.\", \"- **Timer:** per operation. Zero fails the operation. It stays visible, and pulses under 30 s.\")\n\n# difficulty, retry\nsub(\"\"\"**Checkpoints:** every phase is a checkpoint. Failing offers *Retry phase*, *Restart operation*, *Quit*. Retrying a phase restores vitals to at least 60 and gives the phase a fresh time allowance. Phases must be self-contained: a phase's `spawn` lists everything it needs, so `skipTo(phase)` works for retry, dev mode and attract mode alike.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"New Game asks once, in Bea's voice (\"How much do you hate yourself, child?\"), and every chart can change it.\n\n**Checkpoints:** every phase is a checkpoint. Failing offers *Retry phase*, *Restart operation*, *Quit*. Retrying a phase restores vitals to at least 60, the timer to at least 90 s, and the score to the checkpoint's. Phases must be self-contained: a phase's `spawn` lists everything it needs, so `skipTo(phase)` works for retry, dev mode and attract mode alike. Use `ifMissing: true` for what an earlier phase normally leaves behind, such as clamps.\"\"\")\n\n# pads\nsub(\"\"\"**Rumble:** `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` if present, with a Settings toggle. Heartbeat double-pulse at low vitals, a tick per stitch, a click for clamps, a slam for Defib. Guard against a missing actuator; it can't be tested here beyond the guard.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Pads:** accept any pad the browser reports with `mapping === 'standard'`. Read `axes` and `buttons[i].value` directly. If the active pad disconnects mid-operation, pause.\n\n**Rumble:** `vibrationActuator.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` if present, with a Settings toggle. Heartbeat double-pulse at low vitals, a tick per stitch, a click for clamps, a slam for Defib. Guard against a missing actuator; it can't be tested here beyond the guard.\"\"\")\n\n# mouse\nsub(\"\"\"Mouse: hover moves the focus (there's always exactly one focused item), click confirms, wheel scrolls, RMB backs out.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Mouse: hover moves the focus (there's always exactly one focused item), click confirms, wheel scrolls, RMB backs out. In story scenes a click advances the line. In an operation, the wheel's slots and the site tabs are clickable, and the parallax follows the pointer.\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu |\", \"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu. Opens by itself when the tab is hidden (outside sessions) |\")\n\nsub(\"Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement,\", \"Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement,\")\n\nsub(\"| Face (code-driven from clips' events) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression changes |\", \"| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\")\n\n# on its own\nsub(\"\"\"\"On its own,\" a hub phrase, means outside a session: the page runs as a normal game, with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Your brief also says to follow the protocol \"for the game on its own\". In the hub's own check, \"on its own\" means the page opened outside a session, so that's what we mean too: a normal game with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\"\"\")\n\n# session snippet\nsub(\"\"\"  AIHub.on('time-up', finish);                             // within graceMs, host only\n  AIHub.on('end', stopEverything);                         // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n  (function pump() {\n    if (ended) return;\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"\"\",\n\"\"\"  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\n  let ended = false;\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n  (function pump() {\n    if (ended) return;\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\"\"\")\n\n# save\nsub(\"\"\"- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\n- Saves (`src/app/save.js`): progress, best ranks and settings in `localStorage`, wrapped in try/catch. In a session the game saves nothing.\"\"\")\n\n# accuracy of the claim\nsub(\"\"\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A prototype with this stack and these recipes passed the hub's harness at 2 and 4 players (bad network, a player leaving), host-leave and server scenarios, on WebGPU and without it.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"All run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, the §14.3 message rates) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\"\"\")\n\n# install notes\nsub(\"\"\"Fonts: **Barlow Condensed** (500/600/700) for UI and dialogue, **Bangers** for comic lettering (both OFL; credit them on the About screen; about 22 KB each).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"npm warns about install scripts; esbuild works anyway. Don't run `playwright install`: the browsers are already here. Fonts: **Barlow Condensed** (500/600/700) for UI and dialogue, **Bangers** for comic lettering (both OFL; credit them on the About screen; about 22 KB each).\"\"\")\n\n# tests\nsub(\"\"\"Wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` (allow 300 s), and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and **no console line starting `[AIHub]`**. Use a 1280×860 viewport. Run with §16.3 flags and once without them. Then **on its own:**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Wait for `body[data-complete=\"true\"]` (allow 300 s), and require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true` and **no console line starting `[AIHub]`**. Use a 1280×860 viewport. Run all five with the §16.3 flags, and the 4-player run once more without them (WebGL2). Then **on its own:**\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"\"\"- Dev mode: reachable from Pause; each tool runs once without error; a slider changes sim behavior live; Reset restores defaults exactly.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Dev mode: reachable from Pause; each tool runs once without error; a slider changes sim behavior live; Reset restores defaults exactly. Every tuning ID is read somewhere in `src/` (no dead sliders).\"\"\")\n\nsub(\"\"\"One command: **`node tests/run-all.mjs [sim|browser|hub]`**. It prints only failures and a one-line count, and exits non-zero on failure. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Run one browser at a time; \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out, so run fewer. No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. All files stay inside the dev folder.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"One command: **`node tests/run-all.mjs [sim|browser|hub]`**. It prints only failures and a one-line count, and exits non-zero on failure. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. Run one browser at a time; \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out, so run fewer. No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit. All files stay inside the dev folder. Keep a running tally of the bugs your tests catch and which were critical: your brief's Testing Feedback asks for those counts.\"\"\")\n\n# about\nsub(\"\"\"Give each its own pages at ten-foot size: one short answer per page position, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: authored-by model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Give each block its own pages at ten-foot size, a few short answers per page, moved through with L1/R1 or Q/E, never a dense wall. Add a credits page: the model line from your brief, Three.js, Rapier, Bangers and Barlow Condensed (OFL), and the renderer in use this session.\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('ok', s.count('\\n'), 'lines')\nEOF\ngrep -n -E \"Target closed|hub:webgpu|any-pointer|Dies Irae|§12|§13\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-90 | head -20","description":"Apply review fixes to the plan text"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01PN9VY23yELR9C4wtu83X7X":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work"}}}
