{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDEUK5Wvn2Sc8MxEFLA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K9uvJYwdGsbGNkGXCE26Hf","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work/PLAN.md","offset":480,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18928,"cache_read_input_tokens":384878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18928},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"3eba7bea-8fe4-4e12-aae0-aaab1f480ca9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:26.686Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDEU3CcJatZoC7dscvH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01K9uvJYwdGsbGNkGXCE26Hf":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work/PLAN.md","offset":480,"limit":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9uvJYwdGsbGNkGXCE26Hf","type":"tool_result","content":"480\t| UI paper / ink / marigold / alarm | `#F4F1E8` / `#12081A` / `#F2B134` / `#E8443A` |\n481\t| Blood / gel / laser / suture thread | `#C4142F` / `#7CF2C9` / `#FF3B6B` / `#2B6CFF` |\n482\t| Target outlines / marked-hidden | `#39E6E6` / `#F2B134` |\n483\t| Strains body / stave lines | `#2B1456` / `#D7F24A` |\n484\t| Hub seat colors | `#e8443a` `#3b82f6` `#22c55e` `#f5b700` (from the protocol) |\n485\t\n486\t### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\n487\t\n488\t- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(34, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at `(0, 3.55, 1.65)`, looking at `(0, 0.1, 0.06)`. For aspect under 16:9, scale the distance by `(16/9)/aspect`.\n489\t- Subtle life: parallax toward the tip, a 0.2% dolly on each beat, shake on slams, punch-in on Hush, 0.35 s whip between sites.\n490\t- **Drape:** an extruded teal shape at `y = 0.34` with an irregular elliptical window (radii about 1.5 × 0.95, wavy edge). It hides the field's rectangular edge and instantly reads as surgery.\n491\t- **Lamp:** visible in title and story. In the OR it's just warm light.\n492\t- **Lighting:** `HemisphereLight(0xffffff, 0x9aa6b0, 1.5)` and `DirectionalLight(0xfff2de, 1.9)` from upper right, shadow map 2048, `bias -0.0006`, `normalBias 0.03`. Tissue meshes: `receiveShadow` yes, `castShadow` no; otherwise you get wavy acne.\n493\t- Add a low-vitals lamp flicker, and red `danger` from the ink module.\n494\t\n495\t### 9.3 Sites\n496\t\n497\tEach site is a `heightAt(x, y)` sum of Gaussian lobes minus creases, plus two layers of fine sine relief (the relief is what breaks highlights into wet glints), a 1024² painted `CanvasTexture`, and an optional vertex motion. Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement, and `positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)))` for the squeeze.\n498\t\n499\t| Site | Height idea | Base colors | Motion and detail |\n500\t|---|---|---|---|\n501\t| Forearm | One long ridge | `#E8B48F` skin, gash mesh | Slight tremor |\n502\t| Abdomen skin | Gentle dome | Skin, iodine-orange swab paint | Breathing |\n503\t| Bowel | Many tube-like folds | `#E87A8B` | Slow peristalsis |\n504\t| Liver | Two broad lobes, one crease | `#8E2A3A` | Slight squeeze |\n505\t| Stomach | One big dome with rugae lines | `#E9967A` | Churn |\n506\t| Brain | Gyri: sine folds warped by noise | `#E8A9B8`, blue vessels | Nearly still, makes the cuts scary |\n507\t| Heart | Big muscular dome, coronary ridges | `#C4364F`, branching veins | Strong beat |\n508\t| Lung | Two inflating lobes | `#F0A3A8` | Breath every 4 beats moves targets 0.05 fu |\n509\t| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\n510\t\n511\t**Veins:** draw on the canvas with a recursive branching stroke, tapering width (5 lines of code; it looks great in the prototype).\n512\t**Wet glints** (verified): `emissiveNode` with hard `smoothstep` thresholds on `dot(normalView, H)` for two fixed view-space half-vectors (§16.6). Keep glints under about 8% of the area.\n513\t**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends).\n514\t**Scanner:** a world-space circle in the site material's `colorNode`, replacing the surface with cyan-on-navy hatching inside `scannerRadius` (verified).\n515\t**Stave lines:** when a strain is present, five dark lines ink themselves across the organ, drawn on the paint layer, with little note-marks riding them.\n516\t\n517\t### 9.4 Instruments\n518\t\n519\tEach is a small hierarchy of named meshes with `use` animation clips, tilted toward the lower right so it never hides the target, with a springy swing as it moves and a contact shadow. No hands.\n520\t\n521\tScalpel, Forceps (two jaws), Suction wand (hose as a tube), Gel nozzle (foam blobs), Needle driver with curved needle and thread, Laser pen (additive beam, ember at the tip), Scanner puck (with a sweeping ring), Clamp (ratcheting jaws, stays on the bleeder), Syringe (plunger moves), Defib paddles (a pair, sliding in from each side).\n522\t\n523\tCo-op: each seat's tip has a ring in the seat color and a floating name (DOM, `textContent`).\n524\t\n525\t### 9.5 Story staging\n526\t\n527\t- 16:9 stage with a bottom dialogue box and name tag in the character's color.\n528\t- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(30, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at about `(0, 0.2, 12.5)`, busts at about x = ±2.1. Slow dolly. Punch-in plus `speedLines` for shouts (§16.5; it looks exactly like manga).\n529\t- **Five sets** built from boxes and props, inked by the filter: OR 3 and gallery; corridor with rain on the windows; Ward Zero (green tile, pipes); Pip's lab; hospital roof in rain. Bell's office and the boardroom can reuse the corridor shell with new props.\n530\t- Text types out in sync with gibberish voice (§11). Transitions are an ink-wipe across the screen.\n531\t- **Cut-ins:** at big moments, a tilted panel with thick white border shows a close-up of a bust and a comic SFX word (\"KA-THUMP!\", \"FLATLINE!\"). Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else.\n532\t\n533\t### 9.6 Character busts (recipe verified, proportions need your care)\n534\t\n535\tBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. Prototype results: the approach works and looks charming, but with shoulders too narrow it looks like a bobblehead. Use the numbers below.\n536\t\n537\t- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, reshape vertices: for `y < 0`, with `t = -y`: `x *= 1 - 0.27 * t**1.9`, `z *= 1 - 0.1 * t`, `z += 0.06 * t*t`, `y *= 1.06`. Then `z *= 0.94`.\n538\t- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\n539\t- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\n540\t- **Body:** cylinder neck; `LatheGeometry` torso with z scale about 0.62 and **shoulder half-width about 2.1× the head radius**; V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie, cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\n541\t- Portrait inset: render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane.\n542\t\n543\tPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\n544\t\n545\t### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\n546\t\n547\tUse `InstancedMesh` for particles (per-instance color verified). Particles and thread live in a small cosmetic Rapier world on the view side.\n548\t\n549\tThese are not optional; they are what makes it feel great:\n550\t\n551\t- Hit-stop of 60 to 90 ms on FLAWLESS.\n552\t- Forceps: tissue stretches, then a pop, the item arcs, lands and clinks onto the growing tray pile.\n553\t- Grade lettering stamps in at the tip with an ink splat.\n554\t- Hush: 0.4 s freeze, inhale sound, wash expanding from the tip via `hushRadius`; on exit, color floods back with a cymbal swell.\n555\t- Fermata: real silence. On Defib: white `flash`, and music slams back on the downbeat.\n556\t- Strain entrance: stave lines ink in, then the dictionary card.\n557\t- Scrub-in at op start: glove snap, lamp clunk, Bea's line. Rank stamp: a physical 3D stamp, thud, ink, camera kick.\n558\t- Danger: lamp flicker, line boil rising with `danger`, ECG beeps climbing in pitch.\n559\t- Suture thread (Rapier rope) whips and pulls tight. Clamp ratchet. Laser ember and smoke. Gel foam fizz. Blood droplets arc into the suction nozzle.\n560\t\n561\t---\n562\t\n563\t## 10. Animation\n564\t\n565\tUse the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\n566\t\n567\t| Group | Clips to make |\n568\t|---|---|\n569\t| Busts | `idle` (breathing), `nod`, `shake`, `shock` (jump back), `lean`, `sigh`, `bow`, `slump`, `collapse` (Bea, Bell) |\n570\t| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\n571\t| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\n572\t| Strains (skinned) | Adagio `crawl` and `bite`, Tremolo `shiver` and `flee`, Legato `slither` and `jerk`, Crescendo `swell`, Fermata `open` and `close`, Coda `conduct`, `downbeat`, `cue`, `rest` |\n573\t| Organs | Tumor twitch, flap open, lung breath (uniform-driven, clip-timed) |\n574\t| Props and UI 3D | Lamp swing, rank stamp slam, clipboard drop, envelope slide, cut-in panel slide |\n575\t\n576\tTime strain clips to the beat clock: set `action.timeScale` from `bpm` so a bar-long clip always lasts one bar.\n577\t\n578\t---\n579\t\n580\t## 11. Audio\n581\t\n582\tEverything is synthesized in code with Web Audio. No audio files of any kind.\n583\t\n584\t**Graph:** `music`, `sfx` and `voice` buses into a master with a gentle limiter. **Music bus default gain is exactly 0.10**, shown as \"Music 10%\" in Settings. Effects and Voices default to 80%. Write every instrument as a function of `(ctx, destination, time, …)` so the same code runs on `OfflineAudioContext` for tests (verified to render).\n585\t\n586\t**Unlocking:** create the context on boot, and call `resume()` on every keydown, pointerdown and pad press until it runs. Gamepad presses aren't user activation in browser specs, so a pad-only player may stay silent until the browser allows it. If the context is still suspended after a pad press, show a small \"Press any key or click for sound\" note on the Title, and keep trying. Playwright's Chromium here starts contexts running without a gesture, so tests can't prove this path. Note that honestly in your testing feedback.\n587\t\n588\t### Music\n589\t\n590\tA step sequencer with a lookahead scheduler (schedule 120 ms ahead on `ctx.currentTime`). Tempo follows the sim's `bpm`; each quarter note lands on a `beat`. Instruments from oscillators, FM, filters and noise: cello-ish saw, pizzicato pluck, electric piano, choir pad, organ (additive), heartbeat kick, soft hats. Music must be written by you. The one quotation: the first phrase of the medieval plainchant **Dies Irae** (public domain; F E F D E C D D) as Voss's signature. Pip: \"That's the Dies Irae. The Mass for the Dead. She's *signing* them.\"\n591\t\n592\t| Track | Character |\n593\t|---|---|\n594\t| Title | Slow electric piano over the heartbeat kick; Dies Irae hinted in the bass |\n595\t| Story: calm, comic, tense, sad, villain | Short loops; scene data picks one |\n596\t| OR base | Pulsing minor-key bass that tightens as bpm rises; layers enter with phases |\n597\t| Strain layers | Per §5, added on top of OR base while that strain lives |\n598\t| Hush | Low-pass sweep down to about 300 Hz on the music bus, then only heartbeat and one held pad |\n599\t| Fermata | Everything cut; one held organ chord swelling under the flatline tone |\n600\t| Coda | All strain motifs in counterpoint over organ Dies Irae |\n601\t| Credits | The Title theme opened out, major-key ending |\n602\t\n603\t### Sound effects (all procedural)\n604\t\n605\tHeartbeat double thump (pitch-dropping sine), ECG beep, flatline tone, scalpel slice (filtered noise sweep), forceps click, pop, glass clink (inharmonic partials), suction gurgle, gel spray, stitch tick, thread zip, laser buzz (pitch follows power), scanner ping, clamp ratchet, syringe hiss, defib whine and thump, strain chitter and screech, scratch tear, stamp thud, UI move/confirm/back, rain, gallery murmur, door, phone ring, alarm. Rain ambience in story scenes outdoors or at windows.\n606\t\n607\t### Voices\n608\t\n609\tAnimalese/Simlish gibberish, driven by the actual text so a line always sounds the same. Split text into syllable chunks of 2 to 3 letters. Each chunk schedules a blip of about 70 ms: a sawtooth through two bandpass filters, F1/F2 from the chunk's vowel (a: 730/1090, e: 530/1840, i: 270/2290, o: 570/840, u: 300/870), attack-decay envelope, plus a short noise burst for hard consonants. Pitch rises on \"?\", falls on \".\", louder and higher on \"!\". Trigger mouth flaps from each blip.\n610\t\n611\t| Voice | Base pitch | Rate | Color |\n612\t|---|---|---|---|\n613\t| Ren | 190 Hz | Fast | Light, wavers when nervous |\n614\t| Bea | 130 Hz | Slow | Warm, low formants |\n615\t| Bell | 85 Hz | Medium | Booming, slight chorus |\n616\t| Pip | 280 Hz | Very fast | Bright, bouncy pitch |\n617\t| Sorrento | 110 Hz | Medium | Monotone, no contour |\n618\t| Ines | 150 Hz | Medium, clipped | Short blips, hard stops |\n619\t| Voss | 120 Hz | Slow | Breathy noise blended with organ harmonics |\n620\t| Patients | Varied by seed | Varied | Varied |\n621\t\n622\tIn the OR, barks use the same voices, ducked so they sit under the alarm sounds.\n623\t\n624\t---\n625\t\n626\t## 12. Attract mode\n627\t\n628\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the Title, Main Menu or Free Play screens, and on the Touch notice. Reading screens (Settings, About, Lobby, Pause, Dev) don't trigger it. Use wall-clock time, so it's unaffected by slow rendering.\n629\t- **What it is:** the real game, driven by the bot (§15.5) with cheats on: vitals locked, timers frozen, Composure always full, free phase jumps. A corner \"DEMO\" mark and a pulsing \"Press any button\".\n630\t- **Loop (about 3 minutes):** a story snippet (Bea and Ren, S1 lines) → Op 1 shards and stitching → Op 2 incision and clamps → the Hush moment → Adagio laser and forceps → Staccato swarm → Tremolo → Legato with Sforzando → Crescendo and a Fermata Defib → Coda with site switching → rank stamp → logo → repeat.\n631\t- **Exit:** any input of any kind (key, mouse move or click, pad, tap) returns to the screen it came from, at once. It writes no saves and changes no settings. On a first visit it plays silently until the browser unlocks audio, which is expected.\n632\t\n633\t---\n634\t\n635\t## 13. Dev mode\n636\t\n637\tReachable from the pause menu in Story and Free Play. Hidden in hub sessions.\n638\t\n639\t**Standard tools** (each a big button, grouped in pages):\n640\t\n641\t- Jump to any operation and phase; unlock everything; play any story scene.\n642\t- Complete objective; complete phase; win operation; fail operation; force any rank report.\n643\t- God mode (lock vitals); freeze timer; infinite Composure; infinite clamps.\n644\t- Trigger: bleeder at tip, spawn any strain at tip, arrest, Fortissimo, Hush, Sforzando.\n645\t- Time scale 0.1× to 4×; single-step when paused.\n646\t- Auto Surgeon: bot takes over (watch it play).\n647\t- Overlays: colliders and field grid, targets and tolerances, beat clock, frame time and backend name, input monitor (pad buttons and axes live).\n648\t- Render toggles: ink lines, halftone, line boil, shadows.\n649\t\n650\t**Live sliders** with immediate effect, showing the current value and a default tick. **Reset to defaults** on every page, and one that resets all. These are the only source of truth for the values used throughout this plan (`src/config/tuning.js`):\n651\t\n652\t| Page | ID | Default | Range | Meaning |\n653\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n654\t| Hands | `tipSpeed` | 1.9 | 0.8–3.5 | fu/s at full stick |\n655\t| | `stickCurve` | 1.7 | 1–3 | Stick response exponent |\n656\t| | `aimAssist` | 0.35 | 0–1 | Pull toward guides |\n657\t| | `steadyFactor` | 0.4 | 0.2–0.8 | Speed while Steady |\n658\t| Tools | `scalpelTol` | 0.055 | 0.02–0.12 | Cut tolerance (fu) |\n659\t| | `pullTol` | 1.6 | 0.6–3 | Max forceps pull speed |\n660\t| | `suctionRate` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | Volume/s |\n661\t| | `gelRadius` | 0.16 | 0.08–0.3 | Gel brush (fu) |\n662\t| | `stitchGateR` | 0.07 | 0.03–0.15 | Gate radius (fu) |\n663\t| | `laserDps` | 30 | 10–80 | HP/s at full power |\n664\t| | `laserBurn` | 2 | 0–6 | Vitals/s on bare tissue |\n665\t| | `scannerRadius` | 0.3 | 0.15–0.5 | Reveal circle (fu) |\n666\t| | `clampWindow` | 0.18 | 0.06–0.4 | Seconds around a beat |\n667\t| | `defibWindow` | 0.30 | 0.1–0.6 | Gold band width (s) |\n668\t| Patient | `drainMult` | 1 | 0–3 | All vitals drains |\n669\t| | `timerMult` | 1 | 0.5–2 | All timers |\n670\t| | `tempoPressure` | 60 | 0–120 | bpm added at 0 vitals |\n671\t| | `stabilizerHeal` | 15 | 5–30 | Vitals per dose |\n672\t| | `stabilizerCooldown` | 3 | 0.5–8 | Seconds |\n673\t| | `missLimit` | 8 | 3–20 | Misses before failure |\n674\t| Strains | `strainHpMult` | 1 | 0.3–3 | HP |\n675\t| | `strainSpeedMult` | 1 | 0.3–2.5 | Movement |\n676\t| | `spawnRateMult` | 1 | 0.3–2.5 | Notes, scratches, feeders |\n677\t| Gifts | `composureGain` | 1 | 0.2–3 | Meter gain |\n678\t| | `hushDuration` | 7 | 2–15 | Seconds |\n679\t| | `hushTimeScale` | 0.25 | 0.05–0.7 | World speed during Hush |\n680\t| | `sforzandoStun` | 3 | 1–6 | Stun seconds |\n681\t| | `sforzandoDamage` | 0.25 | 0.05–0.6 | Fraction of current HP |\n682\t| | `sforzandoToolMult` | 2 | 1.2–4 | Tool power |\n683\t| | `sforzandoDuration` | 6 | 2–12 | Seconds |\n684\t\n685\t---\n686\t\n687\t## 14. Multiplayer\n688\t\n689\tRead the protocol in full, it's short: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md (Protocol v1, client 1.4.0 when checked).\n690\t\n691\t### 14.1 The decision\n692\t\n693\t**Mode: `shared-world`, seats 1–4, own card.** Surgery together on one patient is the best version of this game: one heart, shared vitals, each surgeon with their own tip and tool. A surgical team splitting between sites, wordlessly, is exactly the drama the source's tone wants. A session round is **Grand Rounds** (§6).\n694\t\n695\tYour brief also says to follow the protocol \"for the game on its own\". In the hub's own check, \"on its own\" means the page opened outside a session, so that's what we mean too: a normal game with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\n696\t\n697\tBecause `AIHub.connect` resolves to `null` immediately when there's no hub, the boot is:\n698\t\n699\t```js\n700\tconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n701\tif (info) startSession(info); else startStandalone();\n702\t```\n703\t\n704\t### 14.2 Rules that apply in a session (`AIHub.active`)\n705\t\n706\t- Straight into the round: no title, menus, attract, story, dev mode or saves. Pause (Options or Esc) opens only a Settings overlay, over the running game. The sim never pauses.\n707\t- Network only through the hub. No chat, emotes or custom names. Show hub names with `textContent` only. Seat color from `info.players[i].color`.\n708\t- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation. Quit and restart do nothing.\n709\t- Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held: that chord is the hub's.\n710\t- If graphics fail, `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n711\t\n712\t### 14.3 Authority and messages (the tested pattern)\n713\t\n714\tThe host's copy runs the only `Sim`, including Rapier. Everyone else renders snapshots. The host's view reads the sim directly; a client reads its decoded state, with entities and other seats interpolated 100 to 150 ms behind. **Your own tip is always local and instant**, and tool sounds and cosmetic trails start locally. Grades and results come from the host.\n715\t\n716\tIf `info.server` is true, the host has no player: no view, no audio, no input, seats from `info.players`, same `Sim`.\n717\t\n718\t| Msg | Direction | Transport | Rate | Contents |\n719\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n720\t| `i` | client → host | unreliable | 12/s | Tip x, y, tool, use, steady, site, sequence number |\n721\t| `a` | client → host | reliable | up to 3/s | Discrete presses: syringe, special, alt, site change |\n722\t| `s` | host → all | unreliable | 10/s | Tick, beat, vitals, timer, tips, moving entities. **Max 1,100 bytes**: larger unreliable messages fragment and are lost whole |\n723\t| `k` | host → all | reliable | 1/s | Full keyframe, under 16 KB |\n724\t| `e` | host → all | reliable | up to 5/s | Batched events: grades, pops, barks, phase changes |\n725\t\n726\tKeep each copy under 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket `send()` wrapper that sheds `s` and `i` first. **Any console line starting `[AIHub]` fails the hub's check**, including rate and size warnings, and `finish` called from a non-host. Drop snapshots older than the newest applied. Clients send `i` even when idle, as the harness needs traffic both ways.\n727\t\n728\t**Run the host tick on `setTimeout`, never on `requestAnimationFrame`:** it must keep ticking with no view (server copy), and at software-rendering frame rates.\n729\t\n730\t```js\n731\t// src/app/session.js, the shape of the skeleton that passed every harness scenario\n732\texport async function startSession(info) {\n733\t  await RAPIER.init();\n734\t  const view = info.server ? null : await createView();    // on failure: AIHub.fail(...)\n735\t  const sim = info.isHost ? new Sim({ op: GRAND_ROUNDS, players: info.players, rng: AIHub.rng('world') }) : null;\n736\t  AIHub.on('card', showCard);\n737\t  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);                       // AIHub.time(): -3000..0, then play\n738\t  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n739\t    if (sim && (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a')) sim.input(from, data);\n740\t    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\n741\t  });\n742\t  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim?.leave(id));           // release what they held, drop their tip\n743\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\n744\t  let ended = false;\n745\t  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n746\t  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n747\t  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n748\t  (function pump() {\n749\t    if (ended) return;\n750\t    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n751\t    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n752\t      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\n753\t      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\n754\t      else sendInputOnSchedule();\n755\t    }\n756\t    setTimeout(pump, 16);\n757\t  })();\n758\t}\n759\t```\n760\t\n761\t**`finish()`** (host, once, on operation end or `time-up`): `standings` as groups of ids, best contribution first, listing every present player; `scores`; `won` (patient alive and operation complete); `stats` (up to 6 entries per player, names up to 16 chars: Cuts, Stitches, Burns, Saves, Accuracy); `awards` (title up to 24 chars, detail up to 40: \"Steadiest Hands\", \"Last-Second Shock\"). If the operation hasn't ended at `time-up`, `won` is false.\n762\t\n763\tA client leaving must not break the round. The host leaving voids it, which the hub handles: show a short message on `end` and stop.\n764\t\n765\t### 14.4 The card\n766\t\n767\tOwn card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\n768\t\n769\t### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\n770\t\n771\tMain Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\n772\t\n773\t### 14.6 Head tags\n774\t\n775\tExact attribute order, `name` then `content`: the hub reads them with a regex. Content must contain no quote characters.\n776\t\n777\t```html\n778\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n779\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n780\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n781\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n782\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Keep the patient alive and finish the operation together\">\n783\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim: right stick or mouse · use: R2 or click · tools: left stick or 1-8\">\n784\t```\n785\t\n786\tDo **not** add `hub:webgpu=required`: the game runs on WebGL2 too (verified). Also add the catalogue tags: `<title>Your Title — Your Tagline</title>` (the hub splits on the dash), `<meta name=\"description\">`, `<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#17707A\">`, `<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:…\">` (an inked heart SVG), `<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">`, `<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">`, `<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\">`.\n787\t\n788\t### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\n789\t\n790\tThese are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\n791\t\n792\t---\n793\t\n794\t## 15. Architecture\n795\t\n796\t### 15.1 Layout\n797\t\n798\t```\n799\tpackage.json            \"type\": \"module\" (Node must import src/sim/*.js as ES modules)\n800\t.gitignore              node_modules/, dist/\n801\tdocs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\n802\ttools/build.mjs         §16.2\n803\ttools/vendor/session.js the hub client, verbatim\n804\tsrc/main.js             the boot branch in §14.1\n805\tsrc/config/             identity.js (title, tagline), tuning.js (§13)\n806\tsrc/data/               ops/*.js, story/*.js, cast.js, sites.js, about.json. Data only, no logic\n807\tsrc/sim/                NO three, NO DOM, NO audio. sim.js, beat.js, scoring.js, physics.js,\n808\t                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\n809\tsrc/view/               renderer.js, ink.js, field.js, paint.js, tip.js, instruments/*.js,\n810\t                        strains/*.js, bust.js, stage.js, fx.js, cutin.js, camera.js\n811\tsrc/audio/              engine.js, music.js, sfx.js, voice.js\n812\tsrc/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\n813\tsrc/ui/                 ui.css, focus.js, hud.js, ecg.js, screens/*.js\n814\tsrc/app/                director.js (screen state machine), story.js, attract.js, dev.js,\n815\t                        coop.js, session.js, save.js\n816\ttests/                  run-all.mjs, sim/, browser/, hub/ (§17)\n817\t```\n818\t\n819\t### 15.2 Sim and view\n820\t\n821\t`Sim` takes seats and per-seat `InputFrame`s (`{x, y, tool, use, steady, alt, syringe, special, site, swap}`), steps at a fixed 1/60 s, and exposes plain JSON-friendly `state` plus an `events` array drained each frame. It has no idea whether anyone is watching.\n822\t\n823\tThe view reconciles meshes against `state` by entity id, and turns `events` into particles, paint, sounds and barks. It runs from `sim.state` in solo and couch play, and from decoded snapshots on a hub client: the same code either way. That single decision makes the Node tests, the bot, attract mode, the server copy and co-op all cheap.\n824\t\n825\t- All randomness in the sim comes from a seeded generator passed in. `Math.random` is banned from `src/sim` by a test.\n826\t- Rapier gave bit-identical results in Node, Chromium, Firefox and WebKit in our test (same 16-digit positions after 1,200 steps). Trust determinism: same seed plus same inputs means same state.\n827\t- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\n828\t- Saves (`src/app/save.js`): progress, best ranks and settings in `localStorage`, wrapped in try/catch. In a session the game saves nothing.\n829\t\n830\t### 15.3 Operations are data\n831\t\n832\tEverything needed to add an operation is a data file. This is the \"normal designer tools\" foundation, along with the tuning table and dev mode. A full example:\n833\t\n834\t```js\n835\t// src/data/ops/broken-glass.js\n836\texport default {\n837\t  id: 'broken-glass', chapter: 1, title: 'Broken Glass', doctor: 'ren', scene: { before: 'S1', after: 'S2' },\n838\t  patient: { name: 'Desmond Pell', age: 52, job: 'Taxi driver', note: 'Has never once used a turn signal.',\n839\t             followUp: 'Discharged Tuesday. Was seen signaling, once, leaving the car park.', bust: { /* §9.6 params */ } },\n840\t  timer: 240, bpm: 72, parScore: 6000, music: 'or-calm', teaches: ['gel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'syringe', 'scanner', 'suture'],\n841\t  sites: [{ id: 'arm', organ: 'forearm' }],\n842\t  phases: [\n843\t    { id: 'clean', objective: 'Disinfect the wound', tools: ['gel'],\n844\t      spawn: [{ kind: 'gelZone', site: 'arm', rect: [-0.6, -0.25, 0.6, 0.25], parTime: 8 }],\n845\t      done: { cleared: ['gelZone'] },\n846\t      say: [{ at: 0, who: 'bea', mood: 'stern', text: 'Gel first, child. Everything in a taxi is filthy, and so are you.' }] },\n847\t    { id: 'glass', objective: 'Pull the glass and drain the wound', tools: ['forceps', 'suction'],\n848\t      spawn: [{ kind: 'shard', site: 'arm', at: [-0.5, 0.1], axis: 30, embed: 0.2 }, /* three more */],\n849\t      on: [{ when: { removed: 'shard' }, do: [{ spawn: { kind: 'pool', at: 'lastRemoved', vol: 0.4 } }] }],\n850\t      done: { cleared: ['shard', 'pool'] } },\n851\t    { id: 'dip', objective: 'Stabilize the patient', tools: ['syringe'],\n852\t      begin: [{ vitals: -25 }, { lockFail: true }],\n853\t      done: { vitalsAbove: 70 } },\n854\t    // ... scanner phase, suture phase, final gel\n855\t  ],\n856\t};\n857\t```\n858\t\n859\tTriggers: `at` (seconds into phase), `when` (`removed`, `vitalsBelow`, `beat`, `bar`, `phaseTime`). Actions: `spawn`, `say`, `vitals`, `drain`, `event` (`arrest`, `fortissimo`), `cutIn`, `music`, `composure`, `wipeToSite`. Completion: `cleared`, `vitalsAbove`, `allClampsOff`, `strainDead`, `arrestsSurvived`.\n860\t\n861\t### 15.4 Observable state and test hooks\n862\t\n863\t`window.__game` always exists:\n864\t\n865\t- `state()` returns `{ screen, op, phase, vitals, timer, score, rank, bpm, beat, site, tool, tips, focusId, promptSet, glyphSet, attract, devOpen, renderBackend, musicGain, tuning, reached: [...] }`.\n866\t- With `?test=1`: `test.step(n)` (advance the sim n steps synchronously), `test.warp(n)` (n sim steps per frame), `test.input(frame)` (override seat 0's input), `test.bot(on, opts)`, `test.skipTo(op, phase)`, `test.hash()` (hash of sim state).\n867\t- `?norender=1` skips drawing for fast UI-flow tests. `?webgl=1` forces the WebGL2 backend.\n868\t\n869\t### 15.5 The bot\n870\t\n871\t`src/sim/bot.js`: `botInput(sim, seat, { noise, reactionDelay, cheat })` returns an `InputFrame`, using only `sim.state`. It has a small behavior for each entity kind, and a priority list: stabilize below 40 vitals → defib if arrested → fire the gift when ready and vitals under 50 → clamp bleeders → objective targets in order. For hidden things it sweeps the Scanner in a raster pattern. It respects tip speed and tolerances, so its results mean something. It powers the playthrough tests, attract mode and dev mode's Auto Surgeon.\n872\t\n873\t---\n874\t\n875\t## 16. Verified recipes and traps\n876\t\n877\tAll run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, the §14.3 message rates) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\n878\t\n879\t### 16.1 Packages"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"36fbf996-609b-46c1-8b1f-deffb66e2799","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:26.847Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work/PLAN.md","content":"| UI paper / ink / marigold / alarm | `#F4F1E8` / `#12081A` / `#F2B134` / `#E8443A` |\n| Blood / gel / laser / suture thread | `#C4142F` / `#7CF2C9` / `#FF3B6B` / `#2B6CFF` |\n| Target outlines / marked-hidden | `#39E6E6` / `#F2B134` |\n| Strains body / stave lines | `#2B1456` / `#D7F24A` |\n| Hub seat colors | `#e8443a` `#3b82f6` `#22c55e` `#f5b700` (from the protocol) |\n\n### 9.2 The operating view (values verified in the prototype)\n\n- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(34, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at `(0, 3.55, 1.65)`, looking at `(0, 0.1, 0.06)`. For aspect under 16:9, scale the distance by `(16/9)/aspect`.\n- Subtle life: parallax toward the tip, a 0.2% dolly on each beat, shake on slams, punch-in on Hush, 0.35 s whip between sites.\n- **Drape:** an extruded teal shape at `y = 0.34` with an irregular elliptical window (radii about 1.5 × 0.95, wavy edge). It hides the field's rectangular edge and instantly reads as surgery.\n- **Lamp:** visible in title and story. In the OR it's just warm light.\n- **Lighting:** `HemisphereLight(0xffffff, 0x9aa6b0, 1.5)` and `DirectionalLight(0xfff2de, 1.9)` from upper right, shadow map 2048, `bias -0.0006`, `normalBias 0.03`. Tissue meshes: `receiveShadow` yes, `castShadow` no; otherwise you get wavy acne.\n- Add a low-vitals lamp flicker, and red `danger` from the ink module.\n\n### 9.3 Sites\n\nEach site is a `heightAt(x, y)` sum of Gaussian lobes minus creases, plus two layers of fine sine relief (the relief is what breaks highlights into wet glints), a 1024² painted `CanvasTexture`, and an optional vertex motion. Use `PlaneGeometry(3.6, 2.5, 280, 200)` with `rotateX(-Math.PI / 2)`, `computeVertexNormals()` after displacement, and `positionNode = positionLocal.add(normalLocal.mul(uBeat.mul(0.03)))` for the squeeze.\n\n| Site | Height idea | Base colors | Motion and detail |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Forearm | One long ridge | `#E8B48F` skin, gash mesh | Slight tremor |\n| Abdomen skin | Gentle dome | Skin, iodine-orange swab paint | Breathing |\n| Bowel | Many tube-like folds | `#E87A8B` | Slow peristalsis |\n| Liver | Two broad lobes, one crease | `#8E2A3A` | Slight squeeze |\n| Stomach | One big dome with rugae lines | `#E9967A` | Churn |\n| Brain | Gyri: sine folds warped by noise | `#E8A9B8`, blue vessels | Nearly still, makes the cuts scary |\n| Heart | Big muscular dome, coronary ridges | `#C4364F`, branching veins | Strong beat |\n| Lung | Two inflating lobes | `#F0A3A8` | Breath every 4 beats moves targets 0.05 fu |\n| Aorta | One thick tube across the field | `#B52A3E` | Pulse wave down its length |\n\n**Veins:** draw on the canvas with a recursive branching stroke, tapering width (5 lines of code; it looks great in the prototype).\n**Wet glints** (verified): `emissiveNode` with hard `smoothstep` thresholds on `dot(normalView, H)` for two fixed view-space half-vectors (§16.6). Keep glints under about 8% of the area.\n**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends).\n**Scanner:** a world-space circle in the site material's `colorNode`, replacing the surface with cyan-on-navy hatching inside `scannerRadius` (verified).\n**Stave lines:** when a strain is present, five dark lines ink themselves across the organ, drawn on the paint layer, with little note-marks riding them.\n\n### 9.4 Instruments\n\nEach is a small hierarchy of named meshes with `use` animation clips, tilted toward the lower right so it never hides the target, with a springy swing as it moves and a contact shadow. No hands.\n\nScalpel, Forceps (two jaws), Suction wand (hose as a tube), Gel nozzle (foam blobs), Needle driver with curved needle and thread, Laser pen (additive beam, ember at the tip), Scanner puck (with a sweeping ring), Clamp (ratcheting jaws, stays on the bleeder), Syringe (plunger moves), Defib paddles (a pair, sliding in from each side).\n\nCo-op: each seat's tip has a ring in the seat color and a floating name (DOM, `textContent`).\n\n### 9.5 Story staging\n\n- 16:9 stage with a bottom dialogue box and name tag in the character's color.\n- Camera: `PerspectiveCamera(30, aspect, 0.1, 60)` at about `(0, 0.2, 12.5)`, busts at about x = ±2.1. Slow dolly. Punch-in plus `speedLines` for shouts (§16.5; it looks exactly like manga).\n- **Five sets** built from boxes and props, inked by the filter: OR 3 and gallery; corridor with rain on the windows; Ward Zero (green tile, pipes); Pip's lab; hospital roof in rain. Bell's office and the boardroom can reuse the corridor shell with new props.\n- Text types out in sync with gibberish voice (§11). Transitions are an ink-wipe across the screen.\n- **Cut-ins:** at big moments, a tilted panel with thick white border shows a close-up of a bust and a comic SFX word (\"KA-THUMP!\", \"FLATLINE!\"). Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else.\n\n### 9.6 Character busts (recipe verified, proportions need your care)\n\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. Prototype results: the approach works and looks charming, but with shoulders too narrow it looks like a bobblehead. Use the numbers below.\n\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, reshape vertices: for `y < 0`, with `t = -y`: `x *= 1 - 0.27 * t**1.9`, `z *= 1 - 0.1 * t`, `z += 0.06 * t*t`, `y *= 1.06`. Then `z *= 0.94`.\n- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\n- **Body:** cylinder neck; `LatheGeometry` torso with z scale about 0.62 and **shoulder half-width about 2.1× the head radius**; V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie, cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\n- Portrait inset: render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane.\n\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\n\n### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\n\nUse `InstancedMesh` for particles (per-instance color verified). Particles and thread live in a small cosmetic Rapier world on the view side.\n\nThese are not optional; they are what makes it feel great:\n\n- Hit-stop of 60 to 90 ms on FLAWLESS.\n- Forceps: tissue stretches, then a pop, the item arcs, lands and clinks onto the growing tray pile.\n- Grade lettering stamps in at the tip with an ink splat.\n- Hush: 0.4 s freeze, inhale sound, wash expanding from the tip via `hushRadius`; on exit, color floods back with a cymbal swell.\n- Fermata: real silence. On Defib: white `flash`, and music slams back on the downbeat.\n- Strain entrance: stave lines ink in, then the dictionary card.\n- Scrub-in at op start: glove snap, lamp clunk, Bea's line. Rank stamp: a physical 3D stamp, thud, ink, camera kick.\n- Danger: lamp flicker, line boil rising with `danger`, ECG beeps climbing in pitch.\n- Suture thread (Rapier rope) whips and pulls tight. Clamp ratchet. Laser ember and smoke. Gel foam fizz. Blood droplets arc into the suction nozzle.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Animation\n\nUse the native system as the base: `AnimationMixer`, `AnimationClip`, keyframe tracks built in code, and `SkinnedMesh` with `Bone` where bodies bend (toon skinning with a mixer is verified on both backends). Don't hand-roll transform tweens where a clip will do; use code only for continuous motion that follows sim values.\n\n| Group | Clips to make |\n|---|---|\n| Busts | `idle` (breathing), `nod`, `shake`, `shock` (jump back), `lean`, `sigh`, `bow`, `slump`, `collapse` (Bea, Bell) |\n| Face (driven by code, not clips) | Blink timer, talk flaps from voice syllables, expression redraws |\n| Instruments | Scalpel press, forceps pinch, suction throb, gel squeeze, needle stitch, laser recoil, scanner sweep, clamp ratchet, syringe plunge, paddles slide-in, charge, slam |\n| Strains (skinned) | Adagio `crawl` and `bite`, Tremolo `shiver` and `flee`, Legato `slither` and `jerk`, Crescendo `swell`, Fermata `open` and `close`, Coda `conduct`, `downbeat`, `cue`, `rest` |\n| Organs | Tumor twitch, flap open, lung breath (uniform-driven, clip-timed) |\n| Props and UI 3D | Lamp swing, rank stamp slam, clipboard drop, envelope slide, cut-in panel slide |\n\nTime strain clips to the beat clock: set `action.timeScale` from `bpm` so a bar-long clip always lasts one bar.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Audio\n\nEverything is synthesized in code with Web Audio. No audio files of any kind.\n\n**Graph:** `music`, `sfx` and `voice` buses into a master with a gentle limiter. **Music bus default gain is exactly 0.10**, shown as \"Music 10%\" in Settings. Effects and Voices default to 80%. Write every instrument as a function of `(ctx, destination, time, …)` so the same code runs on `OfflineAudioContext` for tests (verified to render).\n\n**Unlocking:** create the context on boot, and call `resume()` on every keydown, pointerdown and pad press until it runs. Gamepad presses aren't user activation in browser specs, so a pad-only player may stay silent until the browser allows it. If the context is still suspended after a pad press, show a small \"Press any key or click for sound\" note on the Title, and keep trying. Playwright's Chromium here starts contexts running without a gesture, so tests can't prove this path. Note that honestly in your testing feedback.\n\n### Music\n\nA step sequencer with a lookahead scheduler (schedule 120 ms ahead on `ctx.currentTime`). Tempo follows the sim's `bpm`; each quarter note lands on a `beat`. Instruments from oscillators, FM, filters and noise: cello-ish saw, pizzicato pluck, electric piano, choir pad, organ (additive), heartbeat kick, soft hats. Music must be written by you. The one quotation: the first phrase of the medieval plainchant **Dies Irae** (public domain; F E F D E C D D) as Voss's signature. Pip: \"That's the Dies Irae. The Mass for the Dead. She's *signing* them.\"\n\n| Track | Character |\n|---|---|\n| Title | Slow electric piano over the heartbeat kick; Dies Irae hinted in the bass |\n| Story: calm, comic, tense, sad, villain | Short loops; scene data picks one |\n| OR base | Pulsing minor-key bass that tightens as bpm rises; layers enter with phases |\n| Strain layers | Per §5, added on top of OR base while that strain lives |\n| Hush | Low-pass sweep down to about 300 Hz on the music bus, then only heartbeat and one held pad |\n| Fermata | Everything cut; one held organ chord swelling under the flatline tone |\n| Coda | All strain motifs in counterpoint over organ Dies Irae |\n| Credits | The Title theme opened out, major-key ending |\n\n### Sound effects (all procedural)\n\nHeartbeat double thump (pitch-dropping sine), ECG beep, flatline tone, scalpel slice (filtered noise sweep), forceps click, pop, glass clink (inharmonic partials), suction gurgle, gel spray, stitch tick, thread zip, laser buzz (pitch follows power), scanner ping, clamp ratchet, syringe hiss, defib whine and thump, strain chitter and screech, scratch tear, stamp thud, UI move/confirm/back, rain, gallery murmur, door, phone ring, alarm. Rain ambience in story scenes outdoors or at windows.\n\n### Voices\n\nAnimalese/Simlish gibberish, driven by the actual text so a line always sounds the same. Split text into syllable chunks of 2 to 3 letters. Each chunk schedules a blip of about 70 ms: a sawtooth through two bandpass filters, F1/F2 from the chunk's vowel (a: 730/1090, e: 530/1840, i: 270/2290, o: 570/840, u: 300/870), attack-decay envelope, plus a short noise burst for hard consonants. Pitch rises on \"?\", falls on \".\", louder and higher on \"!\". Trigger mouth flaps from each blip.\n\n| Voice | Base pitch | Rate | Color |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ren | 190 Hz | Fast | Light, wavers when nervous |\n| Bea | 130 Hz | Slow | Warm, low formants |\n| Bell | 85 Hz | Medium | Booming, slight chorus |\n| Pip | 280 Hz | Very fast | Bright, bouncy pitch |\n| Sorrento | 110 Hz | Medium | Monotone, no contour |\n| Ines | 150 Hz | Medium, clipped | Short blips, hard stops |\n| Voss | 120 Hz | Slow | Breathy noise blended with organ harmonics |\n| Patients | Varied by seed | Varied | Varied |\n\nIn the OR, barks use the same voices, ducked so they sit under the alarm sounds.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Attract mode\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the Title, Main Menu or Free Play screens, and on the Touch notice. Reading screens (Settings, About, Lobby, Pause, Dev) don't trigger it. Use wall-clock time, so it's unaffected by slow rendering.\n- **What it is:** the real game, driven by the bot (§15.5) with cheats on: vitals locked, timers frozen, Composure always full, free phase jumps. A corner \"DEMO\" mark and a pulsing \"Press any button\".\n- **Loop (about 3 minutes):** a story snippet (Bea and Ren, S1 lines) → Op 1 shards and stitching → Op 2 incision and clamps → the Hush moment → Adagio laser and forceps → Staccato swarm → Tremolo → Legato with Sforzando → Crescendo and a Fermata Defib → Coda with site switching → rank stamp → logo → repeat.\n- **Exit:** any input of any kind (key, mouse move or click, pad, tap) returns to the screen it came from, at once. It writes no saves and changes no settings. On a first visit it plays silently until the browser unlocks audio, which is expected.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Dev mode\n\nReachable from the pause menu in Story and Free Play. Hidden in hub sessions.\n\n**Standard tools** (each a big button, grouped in pages):\n\n- Jump to any operation and phase; unlock everything; play any story scene.\n- Complete objective; complete phase; win operation; fail operation; force any rank report.\n- God mode (lock vitals); freeze timer; infinite Composure; infinite clamps.\n- Trigger: bleeder at tip, spawn any strain at tip, arrest, Fortissimo, Hush, Sforzando.\n- Time scale 0.1× to 4×; single-step when paused.\n- Auto Surgeon: bot takes over (watch it play).\n- Overlays: colliders and field grid, targets and tolerances, beat clock, frame time and backend name, input monitor (pad buttons and axes live).\n- Render toggles: ink lines, halftone, line boil, shadows.\n\n**Live sliders** with immediate effect, showing the current value and a default tick. **Reset to defaults** on every page, and one that resets all. These are the only source of truth for the values used throughout this plan (`src/config/tuning.js`):\n\n| Page | ID | Default | Range | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Hands | `tipSpeed` | 1.9 | 0.8–3.5 | fu/s at full stick |\n| | `stickCurve` | 1.7 | 1–3 | Stick response exponent |\n| | `aimAssist` | 0.35 | 0–1 | Pull toward guides |\n| | `steadyFactor` | 0.4 | 0.2–0.8 | Speed while Steady |\n| Tools | `scalpelTol` | 0.055 | 0.02–0.12 | Cut tolerance (fu) |\n| | `pullTol` | 1.6 | 0.6–3 | Max forceps pull speed |\n| | `suctionRate` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | Volume/s |\n| | `gelRadius` | 0.16 | 0.08–0.3 | Gel brush (fu) |\n| | `stitchGateR` | 0.07 | 0.03–0.15 | Gate radius (fu) |\n| | `laserDps` | 30 | 10–80 | HP/s at full power |\n| | `laserBurn` | 2 | 0–6 | Vitals/s on bare tissue |\n| | `scannerRadius` | 0.3 | 0.15–0.5 | Reveal circle (fu) |\n| | `clampWindow` | 0.18 | 0.06–0.4 | Seconds around a beat |\n| | `defibWindow` | 0.30 | 0.1–0.6 | Gold band width (s) |\n| Patient | `drainMult` | 1 | 0–3 | All vitals drains |\n| | `timerMult` | 1 | 0.5–2 | All timers |\n| | `tempoPressure` | 60 | 0–120 | bpm added at 0 vitals |\n| | `stabilizerHeal` | 15 | 5–30 | Vitals per dose |\n| | `stabilizerCooldown` | 3 | 0.5–8 | Seconds |\n| | `missLimit` | 8 | 3–20 | Misses before failure |\n| Strains | `strainHpMult` | 1 | 0.3–3 | HP |\n| | `strainSpeedMult` | 1 | 0.3–2.5 | Movement |\n| | `spawnRateMult` | 1 | 0.3–2.5 | Notes, scratches, feeders |\n| Gifts | `composureGain` | 1 | 0.2–3 | Meter gain |\n| | `hushDuration` | 7 | 2–15 | Seconds |\n| | `hushTimeScale` | 0.25 | 0.05–0.7 | World speed during Hush |\n| | `sforzandoStun` | 3 | 1–6 | Stun seconds |\n| | `sforzandoDamage` | 0.25 | 0.05–0.6 | Fraction of current HP |\n| | `sforzandoToolMult` | 2 | 1.2–4 | Tool power |\n| | `sforzandoDuration` | 6 | 2–12 | Seconds |\n\n---\n\n## 14. Multiplayer\n\nRead the protocol in full, it's short: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md (Protocol v1, client 1.4.0 when checked).\n\n### 14.1 The decision\n\n**Mode: `shared-world`, seats 1–4, own card.** Surgery together on one patient is the best version of this game: one heart, shared vitals, each surgeon with their own tip and tool. A surgical team splitting between sites, wordlessly, is exactly the drama the source's tone wants. A session round is **Grand Rounds** (§6).\n\nYour brief also says to follow the protocol \"for the game on its own\". In the hub's own check, \"on its own\" means the page opened outside a session, so that's what we mean too: a normal game with Story and everything else. For multiplayer on its own, Grand Rounds is **couch co-op** for 1 to 4 people on one screen (§14.5). There's no internet play outside the hub, so there's nothing to host or sign into.\n\nBecause `AIHub.connect` resolves to `null` immediately when there's no hub, the boot is:\n\n```js\nconst info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\nif (info) startSession(info); else startStandalone();\n```\n\n### 14.2 Rules that apply in a session (`AIHub.active`)\n\n- Straight into the round: no title, menus, attract, story, dev mode or saves. Pause (Options or Esc) opens only a Settings overlay, over the running game. The sim never pauses.\n- Network only through the hub. No chat, emotes or custom names. Show hub names with `textContent` only. Seat color from `info.players[i].color`.\n- No `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation. Quit and restart do nothing.\n- Ignore Options while Create (button 8) is held: that chord is the hub's.\n- If graphics fail, `AIHub.fail(message)`.\n\n### 14.3 Authority and messages (the tested pattern)\n\nThe host's copy runs the only `Sim`, including Rapier. Everyone else renders snapshots. The host's view reads the sim directly; a client reads its decoded state, with entities and other seats interpolated 100 to 150 ms behind. **Your own tip is always local and instant**, and tool sounds and cosmetic trails start locally. Grades and results come from the host.\n\nIf `info.server` is true, the host has no player: no view, no audio, no input, seats from `info.players`, same `Sim`.\n\n| Msg | Direction | Transport | Rate | Contents |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `i` | client → host | unreliable | 12/s | Tip x, y, tool, use, steady, site, sequence number |\n| `a` | client → host | reliable | up to 3/s | Discrete presses: syringe, special, alt, site change |\n| `s` | host → all | unreliable | 10/s | Tick, beat, vitals, timer, tips, moving entities. **Max 1,100 bytes**: larger unreliable messages fragment and are lost whole |\n| `k` | host → all | reliable | 1/s | Full keyframe, under 16 KB |\n| `e` | host → all | reliable | up to 5/s | Batched events: grades, pops, barks, phase changes |\n\nKeep each copy under 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket `send()` wrapper that sheds `s` and `i` first. **Any console line starting `[AIHub]` fails the hub's check**, including rate and size warnings, and `finish` called from a non-host. Drop snapshots older than the newest applied. Clients send `i` even when idle, as the harness needs traffic both ways.\n\n**Run the host tick on `setTimeout`, never on `requestAnimationFrame`:** it must keep ticking with no view (server copy), and at software-rendering frame rates.\n\n```js\n// src/app/session.js, the shape of the skeleton that passed every harness scenario\nexport async function startSession(info) {\n  await RAPIER.init();\n  const view = info.server ? null : await createView();    // on failure: AIHub.fail(...)\n  const sim = info.isHost ? new Sim({ op: GRAND_ROUNDS, players: info.players, rng: AIHub.rng('world') }) : null;\n  AIHub.on('card', showCard);\n  AIHub.on('start', beginCountdown);                       // AIHub.time(): -3000..0, then play\n  AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => {\n    if (sim && (data.t === 'i' || data.t === 'a')) sim.input(from, data);\n    else if (from === info.host) view?.applySnapshot(data);\n  });\n  AIHub.on('leave', ({ id }) => sim?.leave(id));           // release what they held, drop their tip\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (sim) finish(); });       // within graceMs; a non-host calling finish() warns, and fails the check\n  let ended = false;\n  AIHub.on('end', () => { ended = true; stopEverything(); }); // no input, no sends, audio suspended\n  AIHub.ready();                                           // no key press; don't wait for a first frame\n  let last = performance.now(), acc = 0;\n  (function pump() {\n    if (ended) return;\n    const now = performance.now(), dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25); last = now;\n    if (AIHub.time() >= 0) {\n      if (!info.server) readLocalInput(dt);                // host: straight into sim.input(AIHub.me, …). Client: kept for sending\n      if (sim) { acc += dt; while (acc >= 1 / 60) { sim.step(); acc -= 1 / 60; } sendSnapshotsOnSchedule(); }\n      else sendInputOnSchedule();\n    }\n    setTimeout(pump, 16);\n  })();\n}\n```\n\n**`finish()`** (host, once, on operation end or `time-up`): `standings` as groups of ids, best contribution first, listing every present player; `scores`; `won` (patient alive and operation complete); `stats` (up to 6 entries per player, names up to 16 chars: Cuts, Stitches, Burns, Saves, Accuracy); `awards` (title up to 24 chars, detail up to 40: \"Steadiest Hands\", \"Last-Second Shock\"). If the operation hasn't ended at `time-up`, `won` is false.\n\nA client leaving must not break the round. The host leaving voids it, which the hub handles: show a short message on `end` and stop.\n\n### 14.4 The card\n\nOwn card, in the game's world: OR 3, lamp on, the seat's busts or tips lining up, Title music. It shows the game's name, players in their colors with ready states, how to win, this player's controls, and seconds left from the `card` event. Enter, Cross (button 0) or a click on Ready: `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle (button 3), M, or a click on More Time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round, and there are no menus. Show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()`. The harness sends synthetic keys whose `code` equals `key` (`'Enter'`, `'a'`, `'ArrowLeft'`), so read `e.key` as well as `e.code`.\n\n### 14.5 Couch co-op (on its own)\n\nMain Menu → Grand Rounds → Lobby: four seat cards. Each pad, plus keyboard-and-mouse, can claim a seat by pressing confirm. Seat 1 starts when ready. Same `Sim`, multiple input frames, one screen and camera. Any seat's L1/R1 moves the shared site, with a 0.8 s cooldown. Same seat colors. Seats 1 and 3 have the Hush; seats 2 and 4, Sforzando. (Same in sessions; Hush slows the world for everyone.) On a team result the report shows each seat's stats and awards.\n\n### 14.6 Head tags\n\nExact attribute order, `name` then `content`: the hub reads them with a regex. Content must contain no quote characters.\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Keep the patient alive and finish the operation together\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim: right stick or mouse · use: R2 or click · tools: left stick or 1-8\">\n```\n\nDo **not** add `hub:webgpu=required`: the game runs on WebGL2 too (verified). Also add the catalogue tags: `<title>Your Title — Your Tagline</title>` (the hub splits on the dash), `<meta name=\"description\">`, `<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#17707A\">`, `<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:…\">` (an inked heart SVG), `<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">`, `<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\">`, `<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\">`.\n\n### 14.7 What the hub's own check does\n\nThese are all reproduced in §17: it plays shared worlds at 2, 3 and 4 players at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss, with a player leaving; `scenario=host-leave`; `scenario=server` at 2 players. It checks the client is exactly one unmodified copy (SHA-256, §16.2). Then, on its own: opens the page, presses Enter, Space, Enter, Space, checks that nothing threw, `AIHub.active` is false, `Math.random` is untouched, and the screenshot isn't blank.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Architecture\n\n### 15.1 Layout\n\n```\npackage.json            \"type\": \"module\" (Node must import src/sim/*.js as ES modules)\n.gitignore              node_modules/, dist/\ndocs/AUTHORING.md       how to add an operation, a strain, a story scene, a tuning value\ntools/build.mjs         §16.2\ntools/vendor/session.js the hub client, verbatim\nsrc/main.js             the boot branch in §14.1\nsrc/config/             identity.js (title, tagline), tuning.js (§13)\nsrc/data/               ops/*.js, story/*.js, cast.js, sites.js, about.json. Data only, no logic\nsrc/sim/                NO three, NO DOM, NO audio. sim.js, beat.js, scoring.js, physics.js,\n                        tools/*.js, strains/*.js, ops-runner.js, snapshot.js, bot.js\nsrc/view/               renderer.js, ink.js, field.js, paint.js, tip.js, instruments/*.js,\n                        strains/*.js, bust.js, stage.js, fx.js, cutin.js, camera.js\nsrc/audio/              engine.js, music.js, sfx.js, voice.js\nsrc/input/              input.js (pads, keyboard, mouse → per-seat input frames), glyphs.js\nsrc/ui/                 ui.css, focus.js, hud.js, ecg.js, screens/*.js\nsrc/app/                director.js (screen state machine), story.js, attract.js, dev.js,\n                        coop.js, session.js, save.js\ntests/                  run-all.mjs, sim/, browser/, hub/ (§17)\n```\n\n### 15.2 Sim and view\n\n`Sim` takes seats and per-seat `InputFrame`s (`{x, y, tool, use, steady, alt, syringe, special, site, swap}`), steps at a fixed 1/60 s, and exposes plain JSON-friendly `state` plus an `events` array drained each frame. It has no idea whether anyone is watching.\n\nThe view reconciles meshes against `state` by entity id, and turns `events` into particles, paint, sounds and barks. It runs from `sim.state` in solo and couch play, and from decoded snapshots on a hub client: the same code either way. That single decision makes the Node tests, the bot, attract mode, the server copy and co-op all cheap.\n\n- All randomness in the sim comes from a seeded generator passed in. `Math.random` is banned from `src/sim` by a test.\n- Rapier gave bit-identical results in Node, Chromium, Firefox and WebKit in our test (same 16-digit positions after 1,200 steps). Trust determinism: same seed plus same inputs means same state.\n- Physics runs on the sim side in the flat field space (§3.1). Create a new world per operation and call `world.free()` when done. Don't mutate the world during `step()`; collect, then apply.\n- Saves (`src/app/save.js`): progress, best ranks and settings in `localStorage`, wrapped in try/catch. In a session the game saves nothing.\n\n### 15.3 Operations are data\n\nEverything needed to add an operation is a data file. This is the \"normal designer tools\" foundation, along with the tuning table and dev mode. A full example:\n\n```js\n// src/data/ops/broken-glass.js\nexport default {\n  id: 'broken-glass', chapter: 1, title: 'Broken Glass', doctor: 'ren', scene: { before: 'S1', after: 'S2' },\n  patient: { name: 'Desmond Pell', age: 52, job: 'Taxi driver', note: 'Has never once used a turn signal.',\n             followUp: 'Discharged Tuesday. Was seen signaling, once, leaving the car park.', bust: { /* §9.6 params */ } },\n  timer: 240, bpm: 72, parScore: 6000, music: 'or-calm', teaches: ['gel', 'forceps', 'suction', 'syringe', 'scanner', 'suture'],\n  sites: [{ id: 'arm', organ: 'forearm' }],\n  phases: [\n    { id: 'clean', objective: 'Disinfect the wound', tools: ['gel'],\n      spawn: [{ kind: 'gelZone', site: 'arm', rect: [-0.6, -0.25, 0.6, 0.25], parTime: 8 }],\n      done: { cleared: ['gelZone'] },\n      say: [{ at: 0, who: 'bea', mood: 'stern', text: 'Gel first, child. Everything in a taxi is filthy, and so are you.' }] },\n    { id: 'glass', objective: 'Pull the glass and drain the wound', tools: ['forceps', 'suction'],\n      spawn: [{ kind: 'shard', site: 'arm', at: [-0.5, 0.1], axis: 30, embed: 0.2 }, /* three more */],\n      on: [{ when: { removed: 'shard' }, do: [{ spawn: { kind: 'pool', at: 'lastRemoved', vol: 0.4 } }] }],\n      done: { cleared: ['shard', 'pool'] } },\n    { id: 'dip', objective: 'Stabilize the patient', tools: ['syringe'],\n      begin: [{ vitals: -25 }, { lockFail: true }],\n      done: { vitalsAbove: 70 } },\n    // ... scanner phase, suture phase, final gel\n  ],\n};\n```\n\nTriggers: `at` (seconds into phase), `when` (`removed`, `vitalsBelow`, `beat`, `bar`, `phaseTime`). Actions: `spawn`, `say`, `vitals`, `drain`, `event` (`arrest`, `fortissimo`), `cutIn`, `music`, `composure`, `wipeToSite`. Completion: `cleared`, `vitalsAbove`, `allClampsOff`, `strainDead`, `arrestsSurvived`.\n\n### 15.4 Observable state and test hooks\n\n`window.__game` always exists:\n\n- `state()` returns `{ screen, op, phase, vitals, timer, score, rank, bpm, beat, site, tool, tips, focusId, promptSet, glyphSet, attract, devOpen, renderBackend, musicGain, tuning, reached: [...] }`.\n- With `?test=1`: `test.step(n)` (advance the sim n steps synchronously), `test.warp(n)` (n sim steps per frame), `test.input(frame)` (override seat 0's input), `test.bot(on, opts)`, `test.skipTo(op, phase)`, `test.hash()` (hash of sim state).\n- `?norender=1` skips drawing for fast UI-flow tests. `?webgl=1` forces the WebGL2 backend.\n\n### 15.5 The bot\n\n`src/sim/bot.js`: `botInput(sim, seat, { noise, reactionDelay, cheat })` returns an `InputFrame`, using only `sim.state`. It has a small behavior for each entity kind, and a priority list: stabilize below 40 vitals → defib if arrested → fire the gift when ready and vitals under 50 → clamp bleeders → objective targets in order. For hidden things it sweeps the Scanner in a raster pattern. It respects tip speed and tolerances, so its results mean something. It powers the playthrough tests, attract mode and dev mode's Auto Surgeon.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Verified recipes and traps\n\nAll run here on 2026-11-04: Chromium 153 under Playwright 1.63.0, Three.js 0.180.0, Rapier 0.19.3. A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, the §14.3 message rates) passed the hub's harness on WebGPU at 2 players, 4 players on a bad network with one leaving, host-leave and server scenarios. The 4-player run also passed without WebGPU, on the WebGL2 fallback. The skeleton's scene was small: your real game will take longer in these runs, so allow for it.\n\n### 16.1 Packages","numLines":400,"startLine":480,"totalLines":1204}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01K9uvJYwdGsbGNkGXCE26Hf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
