{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDGFGJtetkHjAT24tHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The read-through found real problems: the packaging grep would false-fail on words inside bundled Three.js, targets could sit under the drape, the idle and bot tests don't fit the unfailable Last Patient, and the playthrough misses some screens. I'm fixing those and the smaller accuracy edits next.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12628,"cache_read_input_tokens":419140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12628},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"39803bbf-51ef-4b5b-9bc9-9dd8378ba81c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:17.363Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDGEzC7YurDbgkpqkQ6","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":2,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDGFGJtetkHjAT24tHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0188dayc8N3uGXxuSfApUMQp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, ('COUNT %d: ' % s.count(a)) + a[:70]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\nsub(\"Four things reviewers criticized in the source, which this design deliberately fixes:\", \"Four things reviewers criticized in the source or its DS original, which this design deliberately fixes:\")\n\n# targets must stay inside the drape window\nsub(\"The tip is clamped to `x` in [-1.55, 1.9], `y` in [-0.95, 0.95].\\n\", \"The tip is clamped to `x` in [-1.55, 1.9], `y` in [-0.95, 0.95]. Anything the player must touch has to sit inside the drape window: `(x/1.4)² + (y/0.85)² ≤ 1`, checked by the data lint in §17. The corners of the rectangle are under the drape.\\n\")\n\n# last stop uses the Hush whoever leads\nsub(\"6. **The last stop:** her heart stops, no warning and no hint. Composure refills. Hush, total silence, one Defib.\", \"6. **The last stop:** her heart stops, no warning and no hint. Composure refills, and the gift is Ren's Hush whoever was leading. Total silence, one Defib.\")\n\n# story input\nsub(\"Delivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Hold Cross/Space to fast-forward; a skip prompt skips the scene.\", \"Delivered as short scenes on a 3D stage (§9.5). Cross, Enter, Space or a click advances; hold to fast-forward; Triangle or Tab skips the scene, with a prompt on screen.\")\n\n# HUD space\nsub(\"The field fills the center, and the HUD holds the edges.\\n\", \"The field fills the center, and the HUD holds the edges. At 1080p the drape window leaves about 100 px clear at the top and 190 px at the bottom, so keep the ECG band shallow and let the portrait use the bottom.\\n\")\nsub(\"| Bottom center | Bea's portrait (live 3D bust, §9.6) and her bark in a comic bubble |\", \"| Bottom center | The current voice's portrait (live 3D bust, §9.6; Bea, Pip in Op 7) and the bark in a comic bubble |\")\n\n# pause in story\nsub(\"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu. Opens by itself when the tab is hidden (outside sessions) |\", \"| Pause | Resume, Retry Phase, Restart Operation, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu. In story scenes: Resume, Skip Scene, Settings, Dev Mode, Quit to Menu. Opens by itself when the tab is hidden (outside sessions) |\")\n\n# rate wording\nsub(\"Keep each copy under 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket\", \"Keep each copy to at most 16 messages/s (the limit is 20, burst 40) with one token-bucket\")\n\n# what the skeleton really tested\nsub(\"A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, the §14.3 message rates) passed\", \"A skeleton with this stack (a toon scene, Rapier on the host, its own card, snapshots at 10/s with a 1/s keyframe, input at 12/s) passed\")\n\n# tests\nsub(\"- Data lint: every op's kinds, sites, tools and speakers exist; every phase has an objective;\", \"- Data lint: every op's kinds, sites, tools and speakers exist; every phase has an objective; every touchable spawn sits inside the drape window (§3.1);\")\nsub(\"- **Bot playthrough on Normal, each operation:** succeeds;\", \"- **Bot playthrough on Normal, each operation (Last Patient has no timer or rank, so it only has to complete):** succeeds;\")\nsub(\"- **Idle:** with no input, each operation fails.\", \"- **Idle:** with no input, each operation except Last Patient fails.\")\nsub(\"using real menu inputs. `state().reached` contains every screen in §8.6.\", \"using real menu inputs. `state().reached` contains Title, Main Menu, Story, Chart, Operation, Report and Credits roll. Other tests here cover Fail, Free Play, Lobby, Settings, About and Touch notice; the hub suite covers the session card.\")\nsub(\"no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder` or `stub` in source or output, no `Math.random` in `src/sim`,\", \"no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder` or `stub` in `src/` (search your own source, not the output: the engines' bundled code can contain those words), no `Math.random` in `src/sim`,\")\n\n# research row\nsub(\"| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; couch co-op on its own |\\n\", \"| Online | AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; couch co-op on its own |\\n| Research | What you actually did, plus this plan's: the AI Hub protocol and harness, engine prototypes on this computer, reference pages on the source |\\n\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('lines', s.count('\\n'), 'words', len(s.split()))\nEOF\ngrep -n -E \"exit-interview|TASK\\.md|STAGE\\.md|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|planner-exit\" PLAN.md; echo \"leak check done\"; grep -c \"§\" PLAN.md","description":"Apply the second round of plan fixes and recheck for leaks"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12628,"cache_read_input_tokens":419140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12628},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"b7a0d0eb-55f2-4920-b999-4c273f2e33a8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:31.661Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDGEzC7YurDbgkpqkQ6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0188dayc8N3uGXxuSfApUMQp":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n