{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDcSN7cw8LJrPkcaN7V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The face now reads as anime, with a tapered jaw and a proper neck, though it's a base rather than a finished piece. Next I'll add the rendered numbers, the render-target flip fix, the screen-UV formula, and the paint-layer mapping to the plan.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2824,"cache_read_input_tokens":461068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2824},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"8e4fabd7-1dfc-4b63-8bf1-a92b6e0e5ea5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:22.767Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDcS22iS8o79jjhFowt","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDcSN7cw8LJrPkcaN7V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M4jBk237vpqY8c5bAu8Yi9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, ('COUNT %d: ' % s.count(a)) + a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# paint mapping\nsub(\"**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends).\",\n    \"**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\")\n\n# cut-ins\nsub(\"Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else.\",\n    \"Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else. **A render target shows upside down on a plain plane unless you flip the plane's UVs** (§16.6).\")\n\n# busts\na = s.index(\"### 9.6 Character busts\")\nb = s.index(\"### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\")\ns = s[:a] + \"\"\"### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\n\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\n\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, then reshape vertices. For `y < 0`, with `t = -y` and `jaw = t > 0.25 ? ((t - 0.25) / 0.75) ** 1.4 : 0`: `x *= 1 - 0.1 * t - 0.42 * jaw`, `z *= 1 - 0.12 * t`, `z += 0.05 * t * t`, `y *= 1 + 0.16 * t`. Then `z *= 0.94` everywhere. `computeVertexNormals()`.\n- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth at y about 340. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\n- **Body:** neck `CylinderGeometry(0.36, 0.44, 0.7, 20)` at `y = -1.18`. Torso `LatheGeometry` through the (radius, height) points (0.34, 0.9), (0.55, 0.82), (1.5, 0.52), (1.95, 0.05), (2.08, -0.8), (2.1, -2.2), placed at `y = -2.08` with z scale 0.62. V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie and cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\n- **Portrait inset:** render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane with flipped UVs (§16.6).\n\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\n\n\"\"\" + s[b:]\n\n# ink notes\nsub(\"Drive all effects through the uniforms. Don't rebuild the graph at runtime. Change `camera.near` or `far` only before calling `createInk`.\",\n    \"Drive all effects through the uniforms. Don't rebuild the graph at runtime. Change `camera.near` or `far` only before calling `createInk`. Screen `uv()` has a top-left origin on both backends (tested off-center), so from a projected tip: `hushCenter.set((ndc.x + 1) / 2, (1 - ndc.y) / 2)`.\")\n\n# render target trap\nsub(\"**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass**\",\n    \"\"\"**Render targets come out upside down on a plain plane, on both backends** (tested with colored markers). Flip the plane's UVs, which was verified upright on both:\n\n```js\nconst plane = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.6, 1.6);\nconst uvs = plane.attributes.uv;\nfor (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\nconst portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\n// each frame, before the inked pass: renderer.setRenderTarget(rt); renderer.render(bustScene, bustCam); renderer.setRenderTarget(null);\n```\n\n**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass**\"\"\")\n\n# screenshot review\nsub(\"Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\", \"Add one HUD portrait and one cut-in: faces must be upright. Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('plan words', len(s.split()), 'lines', s.count('\\n'))\nEOF\ngrep -n -E \"exit-interview|TASK\\.md|STAGE\\.md|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|planner-exit\" PLAN.md; echo \"leak check done\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, pathlib\ns = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md').read_text()\nheads = set(re.findall(r'^##+ (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\.? ', s, re.M)); refs = set(re.findall(r'§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)', s))\nprint('dangling refs:', sorted(refs - heads)); print('code fences balanced:', s.count('```') % 2 == 0)\n# table rows in a block should have the same number of cells\nbad = []\nlines = s.split('\\n'); i = 0; fence = False\nwhile i < len(lines):\n    l = lines[i]\n    if l.startswith('```'): fence = not fence\n    if not fence and l.startswith('|') and i + 1 < len(lines) and re.match(r'^\\|[-| ]+\\|$', lines[i + 1]):\n        n = l.count('|'); j = i\n        while j < len(lines) and lines[j].startswith('|'):\n            if lines[j].count('|') != n: bad.append((j + 1, lines[j][:60]))\n            j += 1\n        i = j; continue\n    i += 1\nprint('uneven table rows:', bad)\nEOF","description":"Update bust numbers and traps, then recheck leaks, references and tables"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2824,"cache_read_input_tokens":461068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2824},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4f41ba1-e4d3-4847-8e93-cb8d40d15190","uuid":"3b9f4c69-bc29-46d2-8797-d045b075bf73","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:40.958Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDcS22iS8o79jjhFowt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M4jBk237vpqY8c5bAu8Yi9":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211920__xe6d801/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, ('COUNT %d: ' % s.count(a)) + a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\n\n# paint mapping\nsub(\"**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends).\",\n    \"**Paint layer:** cuts, scorch marks, gel sheen, smears and stitches paint onto the same canvas, with `texture.needsUpdate = true` when changed (verified on both backends). For a 1024² canvas on that plane, field to canvas is `cx = (x + 1.8) / 3.6 × 1024`, `cy = (1.25 - y) / 2.5 × 1024`.\")\n\n# cut-ins\nsub(\"Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else.\",\n    \"Panels are 3D planes parented to the camera, textured from a `RenderTarget` of the bust (verified per-frame on both backends), so the ink pass lines them like everything else. **A render target shows upside down on a plain plane unless you flip the plane's UVs** (§16.6).\")\n\n# busts\na = s.index(\"### 9.6 Character busts\")\nb = s.index(\"### 9.7 Effects, and the juice list\")\ns = s[:a] + \"\"\"### 9.6 Character busts (these numbers were rendered at 1080p)\n\nBuild each from one parametric function in `src/view/bust.js`. This reads as a cartoon anime face in the ink filter. It's a good base, not a finish, so spend time on hair and clothes. In the prototype, narrower shoulders looked like a bobblehead, and simple chin tapers gave either a ball or a point.\n\n- **Head:** `SphereGeometry(1, 64, 48)`, then reshape vertices. For `y < 0`, with `t = -y` and `jaw = t > 0.25 ? ((t - 0.25) / 0.75) ** 1.4 : 0`: `x *= 1 - 0.1 * t - 0.42 * jaw`, `z *= 1 - 0.12 * t`, `z += 0.05 * t * t`, `y *= 1 + 0.16 * t`. Then `z *= 0.94` everywhere. `computeVertexNormals()`.\n- **Face:** a 1024×512 canvas as the head's `map`. On the default sphere UV, the face is centered at x = 256 (u = 0.25 faces +z). Eyes at y about 232, ±62 from center: white ellipse, gradient iris, pupil, two white highlights, a thick upper lash line. Brows above, a tick of a nose, cheek blush, then the mouth at y about 340. **Expressions redraw the canvas:** states for eyes (neutral, wide, narrow, closed, sad), brows (y and tilt), mouth (6 shapes for talk flaps), plus sweat and tears.\n- **Hair:** a cap (`SphereGeometry(1.06…)` top, forehead edge clamped to a jagged line), a back mass, then 15 to 30 tapered cone locks. This is what makes silhouettes distinct. Use plenty of locks.\n- **Body:** neck `CylinderGeometry(0.36, 0.44, 0.7, 20)` at `y = -1.18`. Torso `LatheGeometry` through the (radius, height) points (0.34, 0.9), (0.55, 0.82), (1.5, 0.52), (1.95, 0.05), (2.08, -0.8), (2.1, -2.2), placed at `y = -2.08` with z scale 0.62. V-neck, lapels, stethoscope, bow tie and cardigan as simple add-ons. Crop at the chest with the camera.\n- **Portrait inset:** render the speaker's bust to a 256² `RenderTarget`, shown on a camera-parented plane with flipped UVs (§16.6).\n\nPatients use the same function with varied hair, skin, age lines and clothes.\n\n\"\"\" + s[b:]\n\n# ink notes\nsub(\"Drive all effects through the uniforms. Don't rebuild the graph at runtime. Change `camera.near` or `far` only before calling `createInk`.\",\n    \"Drive all effects through the uniforms. Don't rebuild the graph at runtime. Change `camera.near` or `far` only before calling `createInk`. Screen `uv()` has a top-left origin on both backends (tested off-center), so from a projected tip: `hushCenter.set((ndc.x + 1) / 2, (1 - ndc.y) / 2)`.\")\n\n# render target trap\nsub(\"**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass**\",\n    \"\"\"**Render targets come out upside down on a plain plane, on both backends** (tested with colored markers). Flip the plane's UVs, which was verified upright on both:\n\n```js\nconst plane = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.6, 1.6);\nconst uvs = plane.attributes.uv;\nfor (let i = 0; i < uvs.count; i++) uvs.setY(i, 1 - uvs.getY(i));\nconst portrait = new THREE.Mesh(plane, new THREE.MeshBasicNodeMaterial({ map: rt.texture }));\n// each frame, before the inked pass: renderer.setRenderTarget(rt); renderer.render(bustScene, bustCam); renderer.setRenderTarget(null);\n```\n\n**Geometry without normals warns under the ink pass**\"\"\")\n\n# screenshot review\nsub(\"Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\", \"Add one HUD portrait and one cut-in: faces must be upright. Look for: text legibility from ten feet, ink quality, overlaps. Fix what you see.\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('plan words', len(s.split()), 'lines', s.count('\\n'))\nEOF\ngrep -n -E \"exit-interview|TASK\\.md|STAGE\\.md|GameTitle|claude-opus|20261104|planner-exit\" PLAN.md; echo \"leak check done\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, pathlib\ns = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md').read_text()\nheads = set(re.findall(r'^##+ (\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\.? ', s, re.M)); refs = set(re.findall(r'§(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)', s))\nprint('dangling refs:', sorted(refs - heads)); print('code fences balanced:', s.count('```') % 2 == 0)\n# table rows in a block should have the same number of cells\nbad = []\nlines = s.split('\\n'); i = 0; fence = False\nwhile i < len(lines):\n    l = lines[i]\n    if l.startswith('```'): fence = not fence\n    if not fence and l.startswith('|') and i + 1 < len(lines) and re.match(r'^\\|[-| ]+\\|$', lines[i + 1]):\n        n = l.count('|'); j = i\n        while j < len(lines) and lines[j].startswith('|'):\n            if lines[j].count('|') != n: bad.append((j + 1, lines[j][:60]))\n            j += 1\n        i = j; continue\n    i += 1\nprint('uneven table rows:', bad)\nEOF","description":"Update bust numbers and traps, then recheck leaks, references and tables"}}}
